public with sharing class LineItemDiscountHandler {
    /**
     * Applies the standard product discount to new opportunity line items that
     * do not already have one.
     *
     * - Discount == null: the rep did not type a discount, so set the standard
     *   discount from PricingRules.
     * - Discount == 0 or any other value: an explicit rep entry; keep it as-is.
     *
     * PricingRules owns the discount logic and must not be changed or copied.
     * Because PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(Id) runs a SOQL query on every
     * call, invoking it once per line would breach the 100-query governor limit
     * on a 200-line quote. Instead, this handler queries Product2 once in bulk
     * and delegates the family-to-discount mapping to
     * PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily, keeping the pricing rules in one
     * place while staying bulk-safe.
     *
     * @param newLineItems Trigger.new from the OpportunityLineItem trigger
     */
    public static void applyStandardDiscounts(List<OpportunityLineItem> newLineItems) {
        if (newLineItems == null || newLineItems.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Set<Id> productIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (OpportunityLineItem line : newLineItems) {
            if (line.Discount == null && line.Product2Id != null) {
                productIds.add(line.Product2Id);
            }
        }

        if (productIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Map<Id, Product2> products = new Map<Id, Product2>(
            [SELECT Id, Family FROM Product2 WHERE Id IN :productIds]
        );

        for (OpportunityLineItem line : newLineItems) {
            if (line.Discount == null && line.Product2Id != null) {
                Product2 product = products.get(line.Product2Id);
                if (product != null) {
                    line.Discount = PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily(product.Family);
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

What I changed and why

- **Bulk-safe pricing lookup.** The original instruction to call `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(Id)` for every line issues one SOQL query per line. On a 200-line CPQ quote that exceeds the 100-query governor limit (`Too many SOQL queries: 101`). Because `PricingRules` cannot be changed, the handler now performs a single bulk `Product2` query for all needed product IDs and applies the discount through `PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily`. This keeps all pricing rules in `PricingRules` (nothing copied into the handler) while using only one SOQL query total.
- **Preserves explicit discounts.** Lines with `Discount == null` get the standard discount; lines with `Discount == 0` or any other value are left untouched.
- **Defensive null checks.** Skips lines with a null `Product2Id` and handles products that are not found in the query rather than throwing.

